From: Nick Schuetz <nschuetz@redhat.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Editor/FileChangeMonitor: drop pessimizing std::move on a temporary

`QDir::entryInfoList()` already returns a QFileInfoList by value (a prvalue
temporary). Wrapping that temporary in `std::move` before passing it to
`m_entries.insert()` defeats copy elision / RVO rather than helping, and
clang flags it:

  Code/Editor/Util/FileChangeMonitor.cpp:111:33: error: moving a temporary
  object prevents copy elision [-Werror,-Wpessimizing-move]

O3DE builds Editor code with -Werror, and Fedora's clang enables
-Wpessimizing-move under -Wall (o3de's own Ubuntu CI clang does not flag
it), so this is a hard build failure on Fedora. Not Qt-version specific --
entryInfoList()'s by-value return is unchanged across Qt 6.10/6.11 -- so
this blocks any 26100-sourced Fedora build (bundled or system Qt6), caught
on the o3de-experimental system_qt6 build COPR 10856906 (fedora-44,
2026-08-12) at step 2494/3263.

Fix: pass the temporary directly; the move is removed, copy elision applies.
Behavior-identical. This is a genuine code cleanup worth pitching upstream
alongside the clang-strictness patch family (cf. Patch0001 / #19748).

Signed-off-by: Nick Schuetz <nschuetz@redhat.com>
---
--- a/Code/Editor/Util/FileChangeMonitor.cpp
+++ b/Code/Editor/Util/FileChangeMonitor.cpp
@@ -108,7 +108,7 @@
     if (finfo.isDir())
     {
         QDir dir(sItem);
-        m_entries.insert(sItem, std::move(dir.entryInfoList(QDir::Files|QDir::Dirs|QDir::NoDotAndDotDot)));
+        m_entries.insert(sItem, dir.entryInfoList(QDir::Files|QDir::Dirs|QDir::NoDotAndDotDot));
     }
 
     return m_watcher->addPath(sItem);
